# Machine-specific zsh config, sourced early by ~/.zshrc (guarded).
# Secrets: seed once from 1Password into the OS keychain (secret seed, map in
# ~/.config/dots/secrets.map), then read instantly and non-interactively:
#   export HOMEBREW_GITHUB_API_TOKEN="$(secret get homebrew-github-token)"
# `op read` also works but costs seconds and needs a TTY — never use it in
# anything a daemon or prompt sources. Never export plaintext tokens here.

# Directory shortcuts for this machine's checkouts:
# hash -d ws=~/work/some-repo

# Extend the prompt (see ~/.zsh_theme):
# RPROMPT_CMDS+=(my_indicator_function)

# Override terminal-title behaviour if this machine needs it:
# term_title_precmd() { ... }
